2192,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When it was the night I was taken on the Night Journey, and I woke up in Mecca, I was terrified by my affair and knew that the people would belie me. So I sat aside, grieving. Then the enemy of Allah, Abu Jahl, passed by and came until he sat with him. He said to him, mockingly: ""Was there anything?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes."" He said: ""What is it?"" He said: ""I was taken on a journey tonight."" He said: ""To where?"" He said: ""To Bayt al-Maqdis."" He said: ""Then you woke up among us?"" He said: ""Yes."" He did not show that he belied him, fearing that he would deny the hadith if he called his people to it. He said: ""What do you think, if I call your people, will you tell them what you told me?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Come, O people of Banu Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy!"" The gatherings rushed to him and they came until they sat with them both. He said: ""Tell your people what you told me."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I was taken on a journey tonight."" They said: ""To where?"" He said: ""To Bayt al-Maqdis."" They said: ""Then you woke up among us?"" He said: ""Yes."" So some of them were clapping (in disbelief), and some were putting their hands on their heads in amazement at the lie, they claimed. They said: ""And can you describe the mosque for us?"" And among the people were those who had traveled to that land and seen the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""So I went to describe it, and I kept describing it until some of the description became confused to me."" He said: ""Then the mosque was brought and I was looking at it until it was placed before the house of 'Iqal — or 'Uqayl — so I described it while looking at it."" He said: ""And with this was a description I did not memorize."" He said: ""The people said: As for the description, by Allah! He has indeed been accurate."""
