2201,Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2201 Arabic Hadees: 1373
2202,Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2202 Arabic Hadees: 733
2203,"(2203) Rabi'ah al-Aslami narrated: ""I used to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he gave me a piece of land, and he gave Abu Bakr a piece of land. Then worldly matters intervened, and we disputed over a palm tree cluster. Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'It is within the boundary of my land,' and I said: 'It is within my boundary.' There was an exchange of words between me and Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr said a word to me that I disliked, and he regretted it. He said to me: 'O Rabi'ah! Say the same to me in return so that it may be retaliation.' I said: 'I will not do it.' Abu Bakr said: 'You will surely say it, or I will seek the Messenger of Allah's judgment against you.' I said: 'I am not doing it.' He said: 'And he gave up the land.' Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the Prophet (peace be upon him), and I followed him. Some people from Aslam came and said: 'May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr! For what reason does he seek the Messenger of Allah's judgment against you when he is the one who said to you what he said?' I said: 'Do you know who this is? This is Abu Bakr as-Siddiq, and he is the second of the two (in the cave), he is the elder of the Muslims. Beware! He may turn and see you supporting me against him, then he will become angry, then he will go to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) who will become angry for his anger, then Allah will become angry for their anger, and Rabi'ah will be destroyed.' They said: 'What do you command us?' He said: 'Return.' Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and I followed him alone, and I kept following him until he came to the Prophet (peace be upon him). He narrated the incident to him as it had happened. He raised his head to me and said: 'O Rabi'ah! What is between you and as-Siddiq?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, such and such happened: he said a word to me that I disliked, and he said to me: ""Say to me as I said to you so that it may be retaliation."" [So I refused]?' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: 'Yes, so do not say it back to him, but say: ""May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr!""' And it is added: ['I said: ""May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr!""'] He said: 'Then Abu Bakr turned away, may Allah have mercy on him, weeping.'"""
2204,Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2204 Arabic Hadees: 1890
